<OmarLayout title="Automations" description="Practical automation for research, data and AI workflows, with clear checkpoints and human oversight.">
  <section class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Automation / 02</p><h1>Less repetition.<br />More room to think.</h1><p class="lede">I’m interested in the work between tools: gathering information, checking it, making a decision and getting the result somewhere useful.</p><a class="button" href="/contact.html?topic=Automation">Bring me a workflow ↗</a></section>
  <section class="section grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">From my work</p><h2>A weekly report,<br />without a weekly rebuild.</h2><p>At BP, I worked on a repeatable competitor-research pipeline for offshore-wind market intelligence.</p><p>Information from Bloomberg and other sources moved through analysis into Excel reporting. The useful part was connecting these steps into a process the team could run again.</p><a href="/work.html#project-3">Read the project context ↗</a></div><div class="panel"><p class="eyebrow">Research pipeline</p><ol class="detail-list"><li><h3>Gather</h3><p>Bring relevant source information into one workflow.</p></li><li><h3>Analyse</h3><p>Organise and interpret the material for the question at hand.</p></li><li><h3>Deliver</h3><p>Produce a consistent report in the format people already use.</p></li></ol></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Where I can help</p><h2>Start with the bottleneck.</h2></div><div class="grid-3"><article class="panel"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Information</p><h3>Research & reporting</h3><p>Source collection, structured summaries and recurring reports that retain a route back to the evidence.</p><a href="/contact.html?topic=Automation&amp;brief=research%20and%20reporting">Discuss reporting ↗</a></article><article class="panel"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Coordination</p><h3>AI & agent workflows</h3><p>Multi-step reasoning, retrieval and tool use, with checkpoints for the decisions a person needs to own.</p><a href="/contact.html?topic=Automation&amp;brief=an%20AI%20workflow">Discuss an AI workflow ↗</a></article><article class="panel"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Integration</p><h3>Connected data</h3><p>APIs, Python and structured data pipelines that move information between systems and reduce repeated handling.</p><a href="/contact.html?topic=Automation&amp;brief=data%20integration">Discuss integration ↗</a></article></div></section>
  <section class="section grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">My approach</p><h2>Make the hand-offs explicit.</h2><p class="lede">A useful automation has a clear input, a checkable output and a plan for when something goes wrong.</p></div><div class="detail-list"><div><h3>Map the existing process</h3><p>What triggers it? Which tools and people are involved? Where does time disappear?</p></div><div><h3>Keep control where it matters</h3><p>Define permissions, review points and what should stop for a human decision.</p></div><div><h3>Test the awkward cases</h3><p>Missing data, failed requests and uncertain results deserve attention before a workflow becomes routine.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section panel"><h2>What are you doing over and over?</h2><p>Tell me the current process, the tools involved and what a useful outcome would look like. Please leave out credentials or confidential records.</p><a class="button" href="/contact.html?topic=Automation">Outline your workflow ↗</a></section>
</OmarLayout>
